ball: if a vertex is outside the ball, its function value cannot be 0 or 2, as this would lead to a contradiction with the lemma's assumptions. Consequently, such vertices must have a value of 1.\\n\\nThis implies the set difference between the universal set and the ball is a subset of the vertices with value 1, leading to an inequality involving cardinalities and the Roman weight. The cardinality of the vertices outside the ball is then bounded above by $m$.\\n\\n\\n**Verifying Inequality Steps**\\n\\nThe proof now utilizes the established inequality regarding vertex set cardinality, combined with lemmas about balls within a graph to deduce `ballWithin G (romanWeight f - 1) c = Finset.univ`. This result implies eccentricity bounds, leading to the final inequality. Each step hinges on standard set arithmetic and graph theory principles.\\n\\nThe proof's completeness is now being checked, with each key step and their corresponding lemmas verified. Initial checks focus on ensuring set membership within the radius-1 ball and examining adjacency. Further investigation aims at characterizing vertices outside this ball.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_unique_two to scratch.lean\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"330\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Append radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_unique_two\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"  have h_sum : ∑ v : V, 1 ≤ ∑ v : V, (f v : ℕ) :=\\\\n    Finset.sum_le_sum (fun v _ => h_ge1 v)\\\\n  rw [Finset.sum_const, nsmul_eq_mul, mul_one] at h_sum\\\\n  rw [Finset.card_univ] at h_sum\\\\n  exact h_sum\\\\n\\\\nlemma mem_ballWithin_one_of_adj {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (c u : V) (hadj : G.Adj c u) :\\\\n    u ∈ ballWithin G 1 c := by\\\\n  dsimp [ballWithin]\\\\n  rw [Finset.mem_union]\\\\n  right\\\\n  rw [Finset.mem_biUnion]\\\\n  refine ⟨c, Finset.mem_singleton_self c, 